-- title:
--   Integral chart function vanishing at ∞ with unit diamond translates
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $L$ a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta=e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)/L$ generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units $\equiv 1\bmod q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Then there exists $b\in K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra $A[j^{-1}]$ of $K$, with $0$-th Laurent coefficient $0$, such that for every $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ other than the identity which fixes pointwise those elements of $K$ whose Laurent series lie in the $L$-subfield generated by the images of the expansions $\mathsf q\mapsto \mathsf q^{d}$ of $j$ for $d\mid q^2M'$, the $0$-th coefficient of $\sigma b$ lies outside $\operatorname{algebraMap}_{A\to L}(\mathfrak m_A)$.
--
--   This provides the modular-unit witness used to separate the cusps above $\infty$ on $X_H(q^2M')$: a function regular on the chart around $\infty$ (integral over $A[j^{-1}]$) that vanishes at $\infty$ while each of its nontrivial diamond translates has constant term a unit. It is the input to the rigidity statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_refl_of_forall_apply_eq_of_forall_coeff_zero_mem_iff_chartAlgInf_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_refl_of_forall_apply_eq_of_forall_coeff_zero_mem_iff_chartAlgInf_xH), which deduces that a diamond automorphism preserving the chart-and-constant-term data at $\infty$ is the identity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_mem_chartAlgInf_coeff_zero_eq_zero_forall_algEquiv_coeff_zero_ne_xH.lean

